A||||6||avengador1||Front sway bar installation||||5||
Z||000000||avengador1||12-02-2001||02:06 PM||||Just how hard is it to take out the front sway bar? I was given an aftermarket bigger front sway bar with all the fittings and I am considering putting the old front one in the rear. What is the easiest way to do the front install? Can I just jack the car up and pull the old one out? What all do I have to remove? This is going to be another of my winter projects and I would appreciate any help you can offer. Thank you in advance.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||12-02-2001||02:34 PM||||Hey avengador!<BR>The sway bar uses a 4 point attachment, one at each A-arm, and one on each frame member...<BR>6 bolts in all, very easy once you get it in the air...||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||12-02-2001||04:27 PM||||Yes, once it is in the air and the wheels are off you just have to wrangle it around the front suspension a little to remove it.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||avengador1||12-02-2001||05:53 PM||||Cool!Thanks guys. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Eriamjh||12-02-2001||06:00 PM||||Uh, you guys forgot to warn him that the bolts that hold the sway bar to the car are likely to break when he removes them.<P>Make sure you spray them on the inside of the frame (theres an oval hole above them for access).  Soak 'em good and long before trying to loosen them.  3 of 4 broke when I pulled mine.||||reg||1
Z||000005||avengador1||12-02-2001||07:16 PM||||Thanks for the warning Eriamjh. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Banzai||12-03-2001||06:52 AM||||Yup, they broke on mine. I used std. 3/8 tap with matching drill bit. I would recommend soaking the bolts through the holes in the frame members, tapping with a hammer, and possibly some heat.<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!||||reg||1
